mplateclustername":"","origin":"proteus","position":"0","createDate":1691007959346,"updateDate":1691007959346}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959346, 1691007959346),
    ($SATQ$1ee7b429$SATQ$, $SATQ$e7180d76-2567-4835-bcce-ca963a7dadf9$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$579398b6-6c72-4f65-9e0d-068a1c4a084b$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Standard English Conventions$SATQ$, $SATQ$SEC$SATQ$, $SATQ$FSS$SATQ$, $SATQ$Form, Structure, and Sense$SATQ$, $SATQ$M$SATQ$, 5, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Bonnie Buratti of NASA&rsquo;s Jet Propulsion Laboratory <span aria-hidden="true">______</span><span class="sr-only">blank</span> data about Saturn&rsquo;s rings collected by the <em>Cassini </em>spacecraft when she made an interesting discovery: the tiny moons embedded between and within Saturn&rsquo;s rings are shaped by the buildup of ring material on the moons&rsquo; surfaces. </p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"e69f1cd9-244e-4e45-b033-fcd4dd94cf4d","content":"<p>studies&nbsp;</p>"},{"id":"364ecc4f-fd3d-4767-b70a-75698d3c3526","content":"<p>has been studying</p>"},{"id":"1866dbc8-9e93-415b-80e1-9a97c0bd6bb3","content":"<p>will study</p>"},{"id":"45b26647-1122-4479-a814-549a8862c003","content":"<p>was studying</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["D"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["45b26647-1122-4479-a814-549a8862c003"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice D is the best answer. The convention being tested is the use of verbs to express tense in a sentence. In this choice, the past progressive tense verb &ldquo;was studying&rdquo; is consistent with the other past tense verbs (e.g., &ldquo;made&rdquo; and &ldquo;collected&rdquo;) used to describe Buratti&rsquo;s discovery. Further, the past progressive tense correctly indicates that an ongoing action in the past was occurring (she was studying) at the same time that another event occurred in the past (she made an interesting discovery).&nbsp;</p><p>Choice A is incorrect because the present tense verb &ldquo;studies&rdquo; isn&rsquo;t consistent with the past tense verbs used to describe Buratti&rsquo;s discovery. Choice B is incorrect because the present perfect progressive tense verb &ldquo;has been studying&rdquo; isn&rsquo;t consistent with the past tense verbs used to describe Buratti&rsquo;s discovery. Choice C is incorrect because the future tense verb &ldquo;will study&rdquo; isn&rsquo;t consistent with the past tense verbs used to describe Buratti&rsquo;s discovery. </p>$SATQ$, false, 0, $SATQ$OSP-625-SEC$SATQ$, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$b41aabbb-a5c7-48a6-b433-38258dc4ff7c$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$proteus$SATQ$, $SATQ$0$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"1ee7b429","external_id":"e7180d76-2567-4835-bcce-ca963a7dadf9","vaultid":"579398b6-6c72-4f65-9e0d-068a1c4a084b","uId":"0e49734f-57ab-48fd-9b74-11621bb6645c","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"SEC","domain":"Standard English Conventions","skill_cd":"FSS","skill_desc":"Form, Structure, and Sense","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":5,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>Bonnie Buratti of NASA&rsquo;s Jet Propulsion Laboratory <span aria-hidden=\"true\">______</span><span class=\"sr-only\">blank</span> data about Saturn&rsquo;s rings collected by the <em>Cassini </em>spacecraft when she made an interesting discovery: the tiny moons embedded between and within Saturn&rsquo;s rings are shaped by the buildup of ring material on the moons&rsquo; surfaces. </p>","stem":"<p>Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"e69f1cd9-244e-4e45-b033-fcd4dd94cf4d","content":"<p>studies&nbsp;</p>"},{"id":"364ecc4f-fd3d-4767-b70a-75698d3c3526","content":"<p>has been studying</p>"},{"id":"1866dbc8-9e93-415b-80e1-9a97c0bd6bb3","content":"<p>will study</p>"},{"id":"45b26647-1122-4479-a814-549a8862c003","content":"<p>was studying</p>"}],"keys":["45b26647-1122-4479-a814-549a8862c003"],"correct_answer":["D"],"rationale":"<p>Choice D is the best answer. The convention being tested is the use of verbs to express tense in a sentence. In this choice, the past progressive tense verb &ldquo;was studying&rdquo; is consistent with the other past tense verbs (e.g., &ldquo;made&rdquo; and &ldquo;collected&rdquo;) used to describe Buratti&rsquo;s discovery. Further, the past progressive tense correctly indicates that an ongoing action in the past was occurring (she was studying) at the same time that another event occurred in the past (she made an interesting discovery).&nbsp;</p><p>Choice A is incorrect because the present tense verb &ldquo;studies&rdquo; isn&rsquo;t consistent with the past tense verbs used to describe Buratti&rsquo;s discovery. Choice B is incorrect because the present perfect progressive tense verb &ldquo;has been studying&rdquo; isn&rsquo;t consistent with the past tense verbs used to describe Buratti&rsquo;s discovery. Choice C is incorrect because the future tense verb &ldquo;will study&rdquo; isn&rsquo;t consistent with the past tense verbs used to describe Buratti&rsquo;s discovery. </p>","parenttemplatename":"OSP-625-SEC","parenttemplateid":"","templateclusterid":"b41aabbb-a5c7-48a6-b433-38258dc4ff7c","templateclustername":"","origin":"proteus","position":"0","createDate":1691007959339,"updateDate":1691007959339}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959339, 1691007959339),
    ($SATQ$1f39ab8b$SATQ$, $SATQ$2045b349-6d92-434e-824d-e7d0dacaa16c$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$696c55b3-5468-4030-b96f-17b8ef4ecbab$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Standard English Conventions$SATQ$, $SATQ$SEC$SATQ$, $SATQ$BOU$SATQ$, $SATQ$Boundaries$SATQ$, $SATQ$E$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>In the novel <em>Things Fall Apart</em> by Chinua Achebe, Okonkwo is a leader of Umuofia (a fictional Nigerian clan) and takes pride in his culture&rsquo;s traditions. However, when the arrival of European missionaries brings changes to Umuofia, the novel asks a central question: How <span aria-hidden="true">______</span><span class="sr-only">blank</span></p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"b3f45c0a-8373-4909-8036-51d46b187ced","content":"<p>Umuofia&rsquo;s traditions will be affected.</p>"},{"id":"63130474-4e20-4509-8461-82443d067820","content":"<p>will Umuofia&rsquo;s traditions be affected.</p>"},{"id":"e306ba10-a7fd-476e-a56c-25e26ab38dd5","content":"<p>Umuofia&rsquo;s traditions will be affected?</p>"},{"id":"074f5d89-f205-409c-80da-7ab6e30e0048","content":"<p>will Umuofia&rsquo;s traditions be affected?</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["D"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["074f5d89-f205-409c-80da-7ab6e30e0048"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice D is the best answer. The clause before the colon tells us that the novel &ldquo;asks a question,&rdquo; so the clause after the colon should be in the conventional form of a question: with the verb before the subject, and a question mark at the end.&nbsp;</p><p>Choice A is incorrect. This choice ends the sentence with a period, which isn&rsquo;t right. The clause before the colon tells us that the novel &ldquo;asks a question,&rdquo; so the clause after the colon should be that question.&nbsp;Choice B is incorrect. This choice ends the sentence with a period, which isn&rsquo;t right. The clause before the colon tells us that the novel &ldquo;asks a question,&rdquo; so the clause after the colon should be that question. In Standard English, questions place the verb before the subject and end with a question mark.&nbsp;Choice C is incorrect. This choice doesn&rsquo;t conform to the conventions of Standard English. In Standard English, questions place the verb before the subject. </p>$SATQ$, false, 0, $SATQ$OSP-KA-BOU-E001$SATQ$, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$15d467a8-095f-4ed1-9087-e84173587199$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$proteus$SATQ$, $SATQ$0$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"1f39ab8b","external_id":"2045b349-6d92-434e-824d-e7d0dacaa16c","vaultid":"696c55b3-5468-4030-b96f-17b8ef4ecbab","uId":"d067219d-a7e4-42e0-bc66-1fb19ac0c569","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"SEC","domain":"Standard English Conventions","skill_cd":"BOU","skill_desc":"Boundaries","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":1,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>In the novel <em>Things Fall Apart</em> by Chinua Achebe, Okonkwo is a leader of Umuofia (a fictional Nigerian clan) and takes pride in his culture&rsquo;s traditions. However, when the arrival of European missionaries brings changes to Umuofia, the novel asks a central question: How <span aria-hidden=\"true\">______</span><span class=\"sr-only\">blank</span></p>","stem":"<p>Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"b3f45c0a-8373-4909-8036-51d46b187ced","content":"<p>Umuofia&rsquo;s traditions will be affected.</p>"},{"id":"63130474-4e20-4509-8461-82443d067820","content":"<p>will Umuofia&rsquo;s traditions be affected.</p>"},{"id":"e306ba10-a7fd-476e-a56c-25e26ab38dd5","content":"<p>Umuofia&rsquo;s traditions will be affected?</p>"},{"id":"074f5d89-f205-409c-80da-7ab6e30e0048","content":"<p>will Umuofia&rsquo;s traditions be affected?</p>"}],"keys":["074f5d89-f205-409c-80da-7ab6e30e0048"],"correct_answer":["D"],"rationale":"<p>Choice D is the best answer. The clause before the colon tells us that the novel &ldquo;asks a question,&rdquo; so the clause after the colon should be in the conventional form of a question: with the verb before the subject, and a question mark at the end.&nbsp;</p><p>Choice A is incorrect. This choice ends the sentence with a period, which isn&rsquo;t right. The clause before the colon tells us that the novel &ldquo;asks a question,&rdquo; so the clause after the colon should be that question.&nbsp;Choice B is incorrect. This choice ends the sentence with a period, which isn&rsquo;t right. The clause before the colon tells us that the novel &ldquo;asks a question,&rdquo; so the clause after the colon should be that question. In Standard English, questions place the verb before the subject and end with a question mark.&nbsp;Choice C is incorrect. This choice doesn&rsquo;t conform to the conventions of Standard English. In Standard English, questions place the verb before the subject. </p>","parenttemplatename":"OSP-KA-BOU-E001","parenttemplateid":"","templateclusterid":"15d467a8-095f-4ed1-9087-e84173587199","templateclustername":"","origin":"proteus","position":"0","createDate":1691007959358,"updateDate":1691007959358}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959358, 1691007959358),
    ($SATQ$1f8cd95f$SATQ$, $SATQ$59a8e1dc-6d62-4b63-93ae-6ceece8028be$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$c427aecb-574c-4ce0-a572-fdf8a05cff43$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Standard English Conventions$SATQ$, $SATQ$SEC$SATQ$, $SATQ$FSS$SATQ$, $SATQ$Form, Structure, and Sense$SATQ$, $SATQ$M$SATQ$, 4, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>In the 1950s, a man named Joseph McVicker was struggling to keep his business afloat when his sister-in-law Kay Zufall advised him to repurpose the company&rsquo;s product, a nontoxic, clay-like substance for removing soot from wallpaper, as a modeling putty for kids. In addition, Zufall <span aria-hidden="true">______</span><span class="sr-only">blank</span> selling the product under a child-friendly name: Play-Doh.</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"2f119aac-e9e0-4d4d-9fc0-333af6ce5bd8","content":"<p>suggested</p>"},{"id":"fda82deb-ff43-4ca4-b3cf-c6765e08d112","content":"<p>suggests</p>"},{"id":"984ba4a9-5e1e-49cc-9ad8-8dd159d55352","content":"<p>had suggested</p>"},{"id":"d6a6bd7f-76d6-4321-a8f6-92fd44af491b","content":"<p>was suggesting</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["A"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["2f119aac-e9e0-4d4d-9fc0-333af6ce5bd8"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice A is the best answer. The convention being tested is the use of verbs to express tense. In this choice, the simple past tense verb &ldquo;suggested&rdquo; properly indicates that Zufall offered her suggestion for the product&rsquo;s name in the past. This verb tense is consistent with the previous sentence&rsquo;s use of a simple past tense verb (&ldquo;advised&rdquo;) to describe Zufall&rsquo;s advice to McVicker in the 1950s. </p><p>Choice B is incorrect because the present tense verb &ldquo;suggests&rdquo; doesn&rsquo;t indicate that Zufall offered her suggestion in the past.&nbsp;Choice C is incorrect because the past perfect verb &ldquo;had suggested&rdquo; isn&rsquo;t consistent with the previous sentence&rsquo;s use of the simple past tense verb &ldquo;advised&rdquo; to describe Zufall&rsquo;s advice to McVicker. Choice D is incorrect because the past progressive verb &ldquo;was suggesting&rdquo; isn&rsquo;t consistent with the previous sentence&rsquo;s use of the simple past tense verb &ldquo;advised&rdquo; to describe Zufall&rsquo;s advice to McVicker.&nbsp;</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, $SATQ$OSP-676-SEC$SATQ$, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$d28cd6df-1876-41de-9f90-510102cb756a$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$proteus$SATQ$, $SATQ$0$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"1f8cd95f","external_id":"59a8e1dc-6d62-4b63-93ae-6ceece8028be","vaultid":"c427aecb-574c-4ce0-a572-fdf8a05cff43","uId":"4df706eb-f358-485e-ad6a-58394cf3d51f","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"SEC","domain":"Standard English Conventions","skill_cd":"FSS","skill_desc":"Form, Structure, and Sense","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":4,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>In the 1950s, a man named Joseph McVicker was struggling to keep his business afloat when his sister-in-law Kay Zufall advised him to repurpose the company&rsquo;s product, a nontoxic, clay-like substance for removing soot from wallpaper, as a modeling putty for kids. In addition, Zufall <span aria-hidden=\"true\">______</span><span class=\"sr-only\">blank</span> selling the product under a child-friendly name: Play-Doh.</p>","stem":"<p>Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"2f119aac-e9e0-4d4d-9fc0-333af6ce5bd8","content":"<p>suggested</p>"},{"id":"fda82deb-ff43-4ca4-b3cf-c6765e08d112","content":"<p>suggests</p>"},{"id":"984ba4a9-5e1e-49cc-9ad8-8dd159d55352","content":"<p>had suggested</p>"},{"id":"d6a6bd7f-76d6-4321-a8f6-92fd44af491b","content":"<p>was suggesting</p>"}],"keys":["2f119aac-e9e0-4d4d-9fc0-333af6ce5bd8"],"correct_answer":["A"],"rationale":"<p>Choice A is the best answer. The convention being tested is the use of verbs to express tense. In this choice, the simple past tense verb &ldquo;suggested&rdquo; properly indicates that Zufall offered her suggestion for the product&rsquo;s name in the past. This verb tense is consistent with the previous sentence&rsquo;s use of a simple past tense verb (&ldquo;advised&rdquo;) to describe Zufall&rsquo;s advice to McVicker in the 1950s. </p><p>Choice B is incorrect because the present tense verb &ldquo;suggests&rdquo; doesn&rsquo;t indicate that Zufall offered her suggestion in the past.&nbsp;Choice C is incorrect because the past perfect verb &ldquo;had suggested&rdquo; isn&rsquo;t consistent with the previous sentence&rsquo;s use of the simple past tense verb &ldquo;advised&rdquo; to describe Zufall&rsquo;s advice to McVicker. Choice D is incorrect because the past progressive verb &ldquo;was suggesting&rdquo; isn&rsquo;t consistent with the previous sentence&rsquo;s use of the simple past tense verb &ldquo;advised&rdquo; to describe Zufall&rsquo;s advice to McVicker.&nbsp;</p>","parenttemplatename":"OSP-676-SEC","parenttemplateid":"","templateclusterid":"d28cd6df-1876-41de-9f90-510102cb756a","templateclustername":"","origin":"proteus","position":"0","createDate":1691007959346,"updateDate":1691007959346}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959346, 1691007959346)
